  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Saturday)\nIssued at 1235 PM CDT SUN AUG 9 2026\n\nScattered afternoon showers and storms will remain in the\nforecast through tomorrow, as the air mass over the region almost\nremains in a \"steady state.\" By late tomorrow, the ridge to our\neast will begin to slightly weaken, sliding to the west under a\nstrengthening trough over New England. This weakened ridge will\nremain along the Gulf Coast through midweek, keeping these\nscattered afternoon showers and storms in the forecast.\n\nUnfortunately, confidence is increasing that this ridge will\nbegin to strengthen closer to Thursday, and continue\nstrengthening into next weekend. Based on the current trends,\nthere's medium confidence in reaching Heat Advisory criteria as\nearly as Wednesday in some locations, with this ridge only\nexpected to grow stronger. By this time next weekend, afternoon\nhighs could reach into the mid and upper-90s, with an extended\nperiod of widespread Heat headlines beginning around Thursday.\n\n/44/",
